# Superpowers docs lifecycle

**This rule is always on.** It overrides Superpowers brainstorming / writing-plans defaults that open a new dated file every time. User/repo instructions take precedence over those skills.

`docs/superpowers/` holds **in-flight decisions and open plans only**. Product / module as-built lives in **`docs/build/`**, **`docs/README.md`**, and module READMEs under `src/` / `core/` / `build/`. This repo does **not** use mogu’s `docs/app|infra|common` four-pillar trees.

## Default: revise in place

1. **Read** `docs/superpowers/README.md` (Active table), `docs/README.md`, and search `docs/superpowers/` + `docs/build/` **before** writing any new spec or plan.
2. **One topic → one living spec.** Prefer appending a `§` section to the existing living file over creating `YYYY-MM-DD-*-design.md`.
3. Put **`Status: active | accepted | landed | superseded`** on the first metadata line of every new or edited spec. Refresh **Updated:** when merging.
4. When a plan is fully done: **same change** move that spec + plan to `docs/superpowers/archive/{specs,plans}/` (keep filenames) and put as-built facts in `docs/build/` (or the module README).
5. Keep `docs/superpowers/README.md` as a **short Active table** + Archive pointer. Do not rebuild a full inventory in `docs/README.md`.

## Gate: when a **new** dated spec is allowed

Open a **new** `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-*-design.md` **only if all** of the following hold:

1. It is a **new top-level subsystem** (no existing living row covers it), **or** an **incompatible fork** of an existing contract that cannot be a section without lying.
2. The author can name, in the new file’s metadata, **which living file was considered** and **why a § merge is impossible** (one short paragraph). If that paragraph cannot be written honestly → **revise the living file**.
3. The topic is **not** any of the ban list below.

### Ban list — never a new hot spec (use living § or as-built)

| Topic shape | Where it belongs |
| --- | --- |
| Subdirectory / scheme C layout / include break / dual-run file moves | Module `README.md` + `docs/build/src-layout.md`, or a § under the owning living (e.g. umbrella SP, tool-event-dispatch, render-rhi-scene) |
| SP1–SP5 / SP1b / SP4b slices of leftover strangler | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-legacy-deep-abstraction-umbrella-design.md` |
| RHI pipeline / frame graph / GPU-process compose / P0 lit | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-render-rhi-scene-design.md` |
| Atmosphere pass + weather domain boundary | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-atmosphere-ocean-cloud-design.md` |
| `app/views` menus + capability dirs | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-views-desktop-shell-design.md` |
| Views 2D CPU frame + RHI present / GDI fallback | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-map2d-frame-design.md` |
| `src/tool` module dirs | `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-13-tool-event-dispatch-design.md` |

### Plans

- **Prefer one plan per living spec** (or per SP checklist already linked from the umbrella). Do not open a plan that only restates a layout move.
- Brainstorming / writing-plans skills that default to a new dated file: **stop** and revise the living Active row instead unless the Gate above passes.

## Don’t

- **Don’t** add Topic 分册 / as-built stub files that only point at a longer design.
- **Don’t** open a parallel dated empty shell when a design already exists.
- **Don’t** treat `docs/superpowers/` as product documentation.
- **Don’t** rewrite archived bodies except mechanical link fixes.
- **Don’t** archive a file when unsure — leave it in the hot directory.
- **Don’t** reopen archived `superseded` / `landed` specs as living twins.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `docs/superpowers/README.md` | Active living table (short) |
| `docs/superpowers/specs/` | `active` / `accepted` living only |
| `docs/superpowers/plans/` | Open checkbox plans |
| `docs/superpowers/archive/` | `landed` / `superseded` |

